{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1401485-fallens-and-spirits","id":1401485,"title":"Fallens and Spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-07T08:16:09-07:00","id":1401485,"title":"Fallens and Spirits?","content":"So there is little talking about the Demon and Spirit or even Umbra in DtF. Almost all &quot;spirit&quot; in Demon refer to ghost actually. So what's their connection?<br /> <br /> Some stuff also use &quot;spirit&quot; to describe Demon. Are they just a special kind of spirits? (To be honest this is a point many people scoff at, Fallens are David's Deer...) <br /> Why doesn't DtF talk about &quot;true&quot; spirits? I think one of the reasons is, the unniverse spirits represent, the Shaman(Werewolf) and Gnostic(Mage) Universe, directly oppose the Juedo-Christian one Demon wields<br /> <br /> Tip: &quot;Demon&quot; refers to evil spirit firstly, especially before the release of DtF, but later it gradually only refers to &quot;Fallen Angels&quot; in DtF","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T08:29:52-07:00","id":1401487,"title":"","content":"So, this is a question about DtF, not MtA? If so, it should probably be moved to the general WoD forum, which handles all gamelines that don't have their own forums. <br /> <br /> From what I recall about DtF, it doesn't really deal with the Umbra all that much: apparently, the demons were imprisoned in the Abyss back before the Umbra was a thing; and as they re-emerge into the world of man, they're encountering it as a new phenomenon. The Fallen Angels from the Abyss, therefore, are not spirits in the sense of the ones we've seen in earlier gamelines like WtA, MtA, and WtO; they exist on this side of the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T10:19:28-07:00","id":1401505,"title":"","content":"It's a question about Spirit which is in MtA(or WtA, whatever) and demon<br /> <br /> So what will happen if they interact with spirit elements?<br /> <br /> Demon is a David's Deer splat, to be honest. They're much like spirit but a separate entity actually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T14:32:41-07:00","id":1401557,"title":"","content":"From a Mage Agnostoc perspective, The Fallen would likely seem to be spirits of the Lower Umbra who embody forces of entropy, torment, and destruction with their maturely highly tied to the nature of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> From a Demon perspective this is due to their Torment and Fall From Grace, although theoretically one could imagine that if they could undo the effects of the horrors of Torment upon them they may be able to regain(?) access to the Higher Umbra.<br /> <br /> This is entirely speculation but perhaps one could imagine that as Fallen are to the Lower Umbra that Angels would be to the Higher Umbra and Watchers/Nephilim/Earthbound/Fair Folk(?) would be to the Middle Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T19:34:39-07:00","id":1401597,"title":"","content":"I won't suprise if the Heaven and Hell in DtF is just a larger realm in High/Dark Umbra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T21:46:29-07:00","id":1401854,"title":"","content":"I would give them the Djinn treatment from Gods and Monsters. Yes, they're spirits. But, they have their own unique qualities that can make them easier to deal with in some ways and far more annoying in others. Need special rites to bind them/immune to a lot of magic outright but *highly* susceptible to Faith (moreso than any other WoD creature). As far as the above talk of torment entropy and destruction it should really depend on the Torment rating of the Elohim. Some Torment 1 rogue angel fighting to save reality from Oblivion really doesn't mesh with any of what Gryffon said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T11:31:31-07:00","id":1401938,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I'm a bit uncertain as to where my points interesect with yours. Not trying to be a hassle but would you mind clarifying for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T17:15:01-07:00","id":1401991,"title":"","content":"Seemed like you were throwing all Elohim into the box of &quot;Oblivion creatures out to end the universe.&quot; Which, even the worst of them, the Earthbound, aren't trying to do. They want to enslave it and stab God to death with it followed by wallowing in whatever sick madness they can cook up. Maybe I misinterpreted it but that's how it came off to me.<br /> <br /> Edit: Seems I only focused on part of what you said. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":".  Reread Gryffon's comment. 07-09-2020, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T17:28:05-07:00","id":1401993,"title":"","content":"Ah, gotcha, I see.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can get where you're coming from, no worries, but let me clarify what I meant to say. Sorry about the confusion.<br /> <br /> What I meant to say is that for demon's their Torment is a representation of entropy and corruption caused by The Fall and everything that came after, particularly their time in The Pit. Even at its least form, Torment 1, it still holds the capacity for growth and taints the entity with shadows of that cosmic harm.<br /> <br /> If one reaches Torment 10, they would probably resemble a servitor of the Oblivion even if they actually aren't. The demon at Torment 10 is unlikely to actively serve either Oblivion or The Wyrm. It simple wants the pain to end and so the world must die.<br /> <br /> That taint, as represented by the Torment, is what I argue represents the infernal nature of the demon and is what keeps it bound to the Lower Umbra and incapable of realizing the ephemeral glory of the Higher Umbra, if it truly is analogous to the fallen's conception of Heaven-Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T13:20:11-07:00","id":1402666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1401485-fallens-and-spirits?p=1401557#post1401557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Mage Agnostoc perspective, The Fallen would likely seem to be spirits of the Lower Umbra who embody forces of entropy, torment, and destruction with their maturely highly tied to the nature of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> From a Demon perspective this is due to their Torment and Fall From Grace, although theoretically one could imagine that if they could undo the effects of the horrors of Torment upon them they may be able to regain(?) access to the Higher Umbra.<br /> <br /> This is entirely speculation but perhaps one could imagine that as Fallen are to the Lower Umbra that Angels would be to the Higher Umbra and Watchers/Nephilim/Earthbound/Fair Folk(?) would be to the Middle Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there's an entire sub-section of the High Umbra filled with demons, who have groups of infernalists and Nephandi as servants/allies.If you're looking for the spirits native to the Middle Umbra, Werewolf is the gameline that really specialises in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T20:08:35-07:00","id":1402719,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that there are demons native to the higher Umbra and entities that you could call 'demonic' or 'diabolical' are essentially in every plane of existence, I was specifically referring to The Fallen of DtF which are obviously not the whole of every being described as a demon in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> So my post was more to say that from the perspective of Demon the Fallen and it's focal entities: Demons are of the Lower Umbra, Angels would probably be of the Upper Umbra, and (this is just my speculation) Earthbound would be of the Middle Umbra with Nephilim of the Penumbra and/or Material World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:30:44-07:00","id":1404055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1401485-fallens-and-spirits?p=1402719#post1402719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that there are demons native to the higher Umbra and entities that you could call 'demonic' or 'diabolical' are essentially in every plane of existence, I was specifically referring to The Fallen of DtF which are obviously not the whole of every being described as a demon in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> So my post was more to say that from the perspective of Demon the Fallen and it's focal entities: Demons are of the Lower Umbra, Angels would probably be of the Upper Umbra, and (this is just my speculation) Earthbound would be of the Middle Umbra with Nephilim of the Penumbra and/or Material World.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to developer commentary the closest thing metaphysically to the Fallen are the psychopomps featured in <i>Ascension</i>, which include the Scarlet Empress/Queen, the Ebon Dragon (both from KoTE and <i>Hunter</i>), Phoenix from Werewolf, and <i>Wraith</i>'s Neverborn. Of course that scenario plainly never happened in &quot;current canon&quot;, so feel free to go wild for your own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:35:32-07:00","id":1404056,"title":"","content":"Certainly; those are also part of the reason why some fans of DtF theorize that the Scarlet Empress/Ebon Dragon may be Angels while the Neverborn are beings of Nothing that got locked outside of Creation and may be remnants of previous cycles of creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:40:11-07:00","id":1404058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1401485-fallens-and-spirits?p=1404056#post1404056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly; those are also part of the reason why some fans of DtF theorize that the Scarlet Empress/Ebon Dragon may be Angels while the Neverborn are beings of Nothing that got locked outside of Creation and may be remnants of previous cycles of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always think this is a common lore<br /> <br /> If you read the Day of Fire, it clearly says there are two Angels spared, and later implies they are Ebon and Scarlett","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:41:13-07:00","id":1404059,"title":"","content":"Certainly and I'm not arguing against it, I'm just saying that to my knowledge it's never explicitly confirmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:43:59-07:00","id":1404060,"title":"","content":"Demon is originally the closing line of CWoD<br /> <br /> VtM, HtR and WtO is obvious <br /> Werewolf are the descendants of a demon (can\u2019t remember well)<br /> Mage are the result of an experiment <br /> Scarlet and Ebon in KotE are the last two remaining Angels<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t know much about CtD and MtR<br /> <br /> <br /> But obviously they do things bad, all lines can\u2019t be mixed very well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:45:12-07:00","id":1404061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1401485-fallens-and-spirits?p=1404059#post1404059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly and I'm not arguing against it, I'm just saying that to my knowledge it's never explicitly confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s up to you finally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:52:25-07:00","id":1404064,"title":"","content":"Aye, which is ultimately the case with most things.<br /> <br /> Canon aside a great deal is written by potentially unreliable narrators and ultimately you run with whatever best suits your tastes and the needs of your story and table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:58:14-07:00","id":1404066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1401485-fallens-and-spirits?p=1404056#post1404056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly; those are also part of the reason why some fans of DtF theorize that the Scarlet Empress/Ebon Dragon may be Angels while the Neverborn are beings of Nothing that got locked outside of Creation and may be remnants of previous cycles of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to <i>Ascension</i> the Neverborn are psychopomps who got stuck in the Dark Umbra when the Shattering happened (unlike the others, who NOPED beyond the Horizon) and are only able to express the destructive parts of Telos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T09:55:04-07:00","id":1405081,"title":"","content":"If I was mixing Mage and Demon, I always felt that the parallels implied mages were humans with strong faith that had a fragment of the divine (god, who IIRC was implied to have shattered and most closely fits with MtA's idea of ascension) but Days of Fire also suggested that some 'avatars' or shards of avatars might have been Angels lost (or obliterated) during the Fallen's war with Heaven (and the angels vanishing may have also been tied to that. I don't recall since its been awhile since I read through all that stuff.) Whil a god fragment might provide faith AND lore (which translate to spheres) an angel fragment would only provide lore (the 'faith' would have to come from a human that way.) <br /> <br /> And as others mentioned the idea of umbral spirits being angels and demons is another viable answer (and does not contradict above) and I believe Ascension mentions psychopomps as a kind of angelic spirit (similar to but not identical to elohim.. serving a different role. Which is also not mutually exclusive with the previous two ideas, I think.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T12:13:47-07:00","id":1405095,"title":"","content":"'demon' really just applies to anything supernatural you don't like. <br /> <br /> The big difference I see is that Fallen are <i>people</i> <br /> Umbrood aren't. They're the spiritual equivolent of AI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}